Work out the inset: a 16px icon needs 4px on every side for 24px, or 14px for 44px.
Check the neighbours. Hit areas may touch but must not overlap; overlapping area does not count.
Make sure no parent clips it. Anything with overflow hidden needs room around the button.
Skip links inside sentences. They are exempt, and growing them steals taps from the text around them.

icon-button.cssCopy icon-button.css
/* The invisible hit area: a 16px icon button, a 24px target */
.icon-button {
/* The hit area is measured from the button. */
position: relative;
}
.icon-button::before {
content: "";
position: absolute;
/* (24 - 16) / 2: reach 4px past the button on every side. */
inset: -4px;
/* Keep the target the same shape as the button. */
border-radius: inherit;
}

Put it on :focus-visible, so keyboard focus always shows it and a mouse click does not.
Keep outline-offset: 0. Both bands then sit on the background outside the component, which is the only place W3C's guarantee covers.
Make each band at least 2px thick. That also meets the size test in 2.4.13 Focus Appearance.
Never write outline: none to swap in a shadow-only ring. Forced-colours mode removes shadows, and the ring with them.

focus-ring.cssCopy focus-ring.css
/* The two-tone focus ring (W3C technique C40) */
:focus-visible {
/* Inner band. An outline survives forced-colours mode. */
outline: 2px solid #fff;
/* Both bands sit on the background, outside the component. */
outline-offset: 0;
/* Outer band: 2px of black around the white. */
box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px #000;
}

Components that already use box-shadow for elevation lose it on focus. List both shadows, ring first.
A global rule loses to component styles. Search the codebase for outline: none, outline: 0 and Tailwind's outline-none.
Outlines follow border-radius in current browsers, so the ring hugs pills and rounded cards.

card.cssCopy card.css
/* A card that already has a shadow keeps it */
.card:focus-visible {
box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px #000, 0 8px 24px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.15);
}

