Black and white are not the only pair. W3C's technique C40 gives the general rule: if the two colours contrast at least 9:1 with each other, at least one of them reaches 3:1 against any solid background.
It is the same maths. The background that hurts most sits halfway between the two colours, where each band gets the square root of the pair's contrast. The square root of 9 is 3. Pick a pair below and the builder shows that worst background and writes the CSS.

